# Fix: managed-rail review dispatches carry an explicit --timeout derived from the sealed wall budget

Defect (dogfood 2026-09-17, campaign blind-review-packet lineage 2): `performFinalPanel` → `performReview` →
`reviewDiff` → `buildReviewArgs` never passed `--timeout` to `scripts/dispatch-review.sh`, whose default is 5m.
All three final-panel seats died rc=124 on a 90 KB diff after ~1h of paid implement/verify/review. A peer
(fleet-comms P3, 2026-09-16) saw the in-loop reviewer die the same way (`terminal_stop phase=full_diff_review`).

Intended behaviour after this diff:
1. `buildReviewArgs` gains `timeoutSeconds` (positive safe integer or null). When set it appends `--timeout <n>s`
   (seconds: accepted by dispatch-review.sh `timeout_to_ms`, GNU `timeout`, and agy's Go-duration `--print-timeout`).
   When null, args are byte-identical to before (dispatch-review.sh keeps its own default) — every non-campaign
   caller must be unchanged. `--timeout` becomes builder-managed: reserved in `extraReviewArgs` like `--endpoint`.
2. `reviewDiff` threads `input.timeoutSeconds` through unchanged.
3. New helper `campaignWallRemainingSeconds(control, observedAt)` reads the SAME limit source as
   `campaignWallBudgetStatus` (`initial_state.limits.max_wall_seconds`) and returns `{exhausted, seconds}`:
   `seconds: null, exhausted: false` when there is no sealed budget (legacy unmanaged loop → no --timeout).
4. Campaign `performReview` (in-rail rounds AND final panel) passes `min(requested, remaining)` or `remaining`.
   Invariant: a seat is never handed more than the campaign's remaining wall seconds.
5. `performFinalPanel` (seats run sequentially) hands each qualified seat `floor(remaining / seats_not_yet_run)`
   — an even split so seat 1 cannot starve seats 2..n; performReview re-clamps so this only tightens.
6. `_runImplementationReviewLoop` terminal review site passes the remainder too.
7. Tests: unit assertions on buildReviewArgs (emit / omit / reject 0,negative,float,string / reserved flag);
   dogfood kill→resume campaign asserts every review dispatch (in-loop + single panel seat) carries `--timeout 115s`
   (cap 120 s, clock 01:00:00 → 01:00:05). The dogfood fixture's qc seat runner was switched `fixture`→`cc-shim`
   (and roster.reviewer_runner to match) because v2.36.58 intake now refuses non-blind-capable qc runners; that
   fixture had been red since v2.36.58.

Out of scope: rail defect (2) graph-check 14400 vs schema 7200 wall cap; receipt keys (`packet_hash`, 1a-B);
any change to dispatch-review.sh defaults.

Review for: correctness of the remaining-budget math and edge cases (exhausted → block, null → no flag,
requested>remaining clamp, seatsNotYetRun counting when unqualified seats are interleaved), whether any existing
caller's args changed shape, whether the even split can produce a value < 1 or a wrong index in the
`finalPanelSeatQualified(roster, later, index + offset)` call, test vacuity (do the assertions really pin the
behaviour), and anything the diff claims but does not do.

